---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const pageTitle = "Doors & Entry Systems | Appalachian Sheds Inc. \u2014 Source-Fidelity Review";
const pageDescription = "";
---
<Base title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
<Fragment set:html={"<section aria-labelledby=\"asi-doors-final-title\" id=\"asi-doors-final\">\n<div class=\"adf-shell\">\n<div class=\"asi-source-alert\" role=\"note\">Door configurations below follow the original four-family ASI Doors &amp; Entry Systems source. The listed dollar figures are historical installed planning references, not verified current selling prices or a substitute for a written proposal. Images are reserved for real door-option photographs and will be added after verification.</div><header class=\"adf-head\">\n<p class=\"adf-kicker\">Options &amp; Upgrades \u00b7 Doors &amp; Entry Systems</p>\n<h2 class=\"adf-title\" id=\"asi-doors-final-title\">Choose the Door That Fits the Way You Will Use the Building</h2>\n<p class=\"adf-subtitle\">Access \u00b7 Security \u00b7 Weather Protection \u00b7 Architectural Character</p>\n<p class=\"adf-lede\">The door affects daily access, equipment movement, security, weather protection, threshold comfort, wall layout and how finished the building feels. Appalachian Sheds focuses this category on four practical door families so homeowners can compare function first, then select the architectural style that best fits the building.</p>\n<div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"adf-divider\"></div>\n</header>\n<nav aria-label=\"Door option categories\" class=\"adf-category-nav\">\n<a href=\"#asi-door-wood\"><strong>Wood Doors</strong><span>Door Option 01</span></a>\n<a href=\"#asi-door-fiberglass-slab\"><strong>Fiberglass Solid Slab Doors</strong><span>Door Option 02</span></a>\n<a href=\"#asi-door-prehung-fiberglass\"><strong>Prehung Fiberglass Entry Doors</strong><span>Door Option 03</span></a>\n<a href=\"#asi-door-carriage\"><strong>Architectural Carriage-Style Double Doors</strong><span>Door Option 04</span></a>\n</nav>\n<div class=\"adf-intro-grid\">\n<section class=\"adf-intro-card\">\n<h3>Start With What the Building Must Do</h3>\n<p>A basic storage building, workshop, garden building and backyard office do not need the same entry system. The right starting point is the intended use and the largest item that must move through the opening.</p>\n<p>Door selection should happen before the rough opening, header, siding layout, trim, threshold, ramp or landing and interior wall use are finalized.</p>\n<style>\n.asi-arch-xref{width:94%!important;max-width:1440px!important;margin:28px auto!important;padding:26px 24px!important;background:#E4E1DB!important;border-left:5px solid #C9A06C!important;color:#2B3030!important;font-family:'Montserrat',Arial,sans-serif!important;font-style:italic!important}\n.asi-arch-xref *{font-family:'Montserrat',Arial,sans-serif!important;font-style:italic!important;box-sizing:border-box!important;border-radius:0!important}\n.asi-arch-xref strong{display:block!important;margin:0 0 8px!important;font-weight:900!important;font-size:12px!important}\n.asi-arch-xref p{margin:0 0 12px!important;font-weight:800!important;font-size:11px!important;line-height:1.6!important}\n.asi-arch-xref a{display:inline-block!important;padding-bottom:3px!important;border-bottom:2px solid #C9A06C!important;color:#2B3030!important;font-weight:900!important;font-size:10px!important;letter-spacing:.07em!important;text-transform:uppercase!important;text-decoration:none!important}\n</style>\n<div class=\"asi-arch-xref\">\n<strong>Need Weather Protection Over the Entry?</strong>\n<p>Door slabs, hardware and glazing remain in this category. Structural door awnings, entry canopies and porch roofs are designed and priced in the Porches, Awnings, Dormers &amp; Architectural Roofline Options category.</p>\n<a href=\"/porches-awnings-dormers-roofline-options/\">Review Entry Awnings &amp; Porches</a>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"adf-intro-card\">\n<h3>Door Family Before Door Style</h3>\n<p>Wood doors, exterior-hinged fiberglass slab doors and prehung residential fiberglass doors may look similar from a distance, but they are not the same wall-opening system.</p>\n<p>The written project scope controls the final door material, size, hardware, glazing, finish responsibility and standard-versus-upgrade status.</p>\n</section>\n</div>\n<div aria-label=\"Door planning sequence\" class=\"adf-sequence\">\n<div><b>1</b><strong>Intended Use</strong><span>Storage, workshop, office, studio, garden building or specialty use.</span></div>\n<div><b>2</b><strong>Access Need</strong><span>Pedestrian entry, mower, cart, tools, workbench or other equipment.</span></div>\n<div><b>3</b><strong>Door Family</strong><span>Wood, fiberglass slab, prehung fiberglass or architectural carriage-style.</span></div>\n<div><b>4</b><strong>Opening &amp; Finish</strong><span>Rough opening, threshold, swing, ramp, hardware, flashing, trim and finish.</span></div>\n</div>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"asi-door-wood-title\" class=\"adf-option\" id=\"asi-door-wood\">\n<div class=\"adf-option-head\">\n<div class=\"adf-option-copy\">\n<span class=\"adf-mini\">Door Option 01</span>\n<h3 id=\"asi-door-wood-title\">Wood Doors</h3>\n<p>Wood doors provide the most traditional shed, cottage and Appalachian character in the door lineup. They are particularly well suited to Classic sheds, garden buildings, barn-inspired structures and projects where the entry should feel integrated with the siding and trim rather than like a residential house door added to a shed.</p>\n<p>Wood also requires the clearest maintenance expectations. Exterior wood doors must be properly finished and maintained so the door, joints, edges and hardware remain protected from weather exposure.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"adf-option-character\">\n<span class=\"adf-character-label\">Architectural Character</span>\n<h3>Traditional. Crafted. Warm. Appalachian.</h3>\n<p>The strongest fit for homeowners who want authentic shed or barn character and are comfortable with the maintenance responsibilities that come with exterior wood.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"adf-two-grid\">\n<section class=\"adf-panel\">\n<h4>Typical Wood-Door Considerations</h4>\n<ul class=\"adf-list\">\n<li>Single or double configurations depending upon access needs</li>\n<li>Exterior hinges sized for the door weight and width</li>\n<li>Secure latch or keyed hardware as specified</li>\n<li>Threshold, sill and water-management details coordinated with the opening</li>\n<li>Ramp or landing sized to the usable opening where required</li>\n<li>Paint, stain or protective finish maintained throughout service life</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"adf-panel\">\n<h4>Best Uses</h4>\n<ul class=\"adf-list\">\n<li>Basic and premium storage buildings</li>\n<li>Garden buildings and cottages</li>\n<li>Traditional wide double-door storage access</li>\n<li>Barn-inspired structures</li>\n<li>Front-facing buildings where the door is part of the architectural character</li>\n<li>Projects where natural wood character is preferred over residential-entry styling</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</div>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"adf-wood-price-title\" class=\"adf-pricing\">\n<div class=\"adf-pricing-head\">\n<h4 id=\"adf-wood-price-title\">Wood Door Planning Prices</h4>\n<p>The following installed planning prices are carried forward from the Appalachian Sheds source information. Final project pricing is controlled by the current written scope.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"adf-table-wrap\">\n<table class=\"adf-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\">Wood Door Option</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Installed Planning Price</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Best For</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Planning Note</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d01-01\">36\" Single Wood Door</a></td><td>$390</td><td>Basic storage and simple garden buildings</td><td>Most economical traditional door path</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d01-02\">Double Wood Doors</a></td><td>$690</td><td>Mowers, carts, tools and wider storage access</td><td>Good value where equipment movement matters</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d01-03\">Double Colonial Wood Doors</a></td><td>$930</td><td>More finished traditional elevations</td><td>Stronger front-facing appearance</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d01-04\">Double Wood Doors with Transom Windows</a></td><td>$1,110</td><td>Storage or workshop with additional daylight</td><td>Transoms add light without making the doors fully glazed</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d01-05\">Double Colonial Wood Doors with Transom Windows</a></td><td>$1,380</td><td>Cottage and garden-building character</td><td>Combines traditional detailing with added light</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d01-06\">Single Arched Wood Door 36\"</a></td><td>$1,020</td><td>Cottage, garden and specialty buildings</td><td>Best when the entry is intentionally featured</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"adf-price-note\">Carriage-style double doors are presented separately as Door Option 04 because they represent a distinct premium architectural category.</p>\n</section>\n<div class=\"asi-photo-group\"><div class=\"asi-photo-head\"><p class=\"asi-photo-eyebrow\">Door Appearance Reference \u00b7 Photography To Be Added</p><h4>Compare the Actual Door Configurations</h4><p>Each position is reserved for a photograph of the exact door option named below. Photographs will be supplied by Appalachian Sheds; no conceptual substitute is shown.</p></div><div class=\"asi-door-gallery\"><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d01-01\"><div aria-label='Photograph pending: 36\" Single Wood Door' class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D01-01 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>36\" Single Wood Door</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d01-02\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: Double Wood Doors\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D01-02 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>Double Wood Doors</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d01-03\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: Double Colonial Wood Doors\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D01-03 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>Double Colonial Wood Doors</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d01-04\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: Double Wood Doors with Transom Windows\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D01-04 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>Double Wood Doors with Transom Windows</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d01-05\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: Double Colonial Wood Doors with Transom Windows\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D01-05 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>Double Colonial Wood Doors with Transom Windows</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d01-06\"><div aria-label='Photograph pending: Single Arched Wood Door 36\"' class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D01-06 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>Single Arched Wood Door 36\"</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure></div></div></section>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"asi-door-fiberglass-slab-title\" class=\"adf-option\" id=\"asi-door-fiberglass-slab\">\n<div class=\"adf-option-head\">\n<div class=\"adf-option-copy\">\n<span class=\"adf-mini\">Door Option 02</span>\n<h3 id=\"asi-door-fiberglass-slab-title\">Fiberglass Solid Slab Doors with Exterior Hinges</h3>\n<p>This door system uses a fiberglass slab in a shed-style exterior-hinged opening rather than a conventional residential prehung jamb system. It offers a cleaner, more stable and lower-maintenance door face while preserving the straightforward operating character of a shed door.</p>\n<p>The exterior hinges remain visible and the opening, trim, threshold and latch hardware are integrated into the building. This makes the system distinctly different from the residential-style prehung entry doors shown in Option 03.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"adf-option-character\">\n<span class=\"adf-character-label\">Architectural Character</span>\n<h3>Durable. Practical. Clean. Shed-Appropriate.</h3>\n<p>A strong middle path for homeowners who want fiberglass durability without making the building look or operate like a house entry.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"adf-two-grid\">\n<section class=\"adf-panel\">\n<h4>How the System Is Built</h4>\n<ul class=\"adf-list\">\n<li>Fiberglass slab rather than a complete prehung jamb unit</li>\n<li>Exterior-mounted hinges remain visible</li>\n<li>Door opening and trim are constructed as part of the shed wall system</li>\n<li>Threshold and water-management details are coordinated with the building</li>\n<li>Single- and double-door configurations may be used</li>\n<li>Glass-lite slab choices can add daylight where desired</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"adf-panel\">\n<h4>Best Uses</h4>\n<ul class=\"adf-list\">\n<li>Workshops and hobby buildings</li>\n<li>Upgraded utility buildings</li>\n<li>Garden rooms and storage buildings</li>\n<li>Customers wanting less wood-door maintenance</li>\n<li>Double-door access for mower and equipment storage</li>\n<li>Projects where a house-door appearance would feel unnecessarily residential</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</div>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"adf-slab-price-title\" class=\"adf-pricing\">\n<div class=\"adf-pricing-head\">\n<h4 id=\"adf-slab-price-title\">Fiberglass Slab Door Planning Prices</h4>\n<p>These installed planning prices come directly from the supplied Appalachian Sheds door source.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"adf-table-wrap\">\n<table class=\"adf-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\">Fiberglass Slab Option</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Installed Planning Price</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Best For</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Planning Note</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d02-01\">Single Fiberglass Slab Door</a></td><td>$630</td><td>Workshops and upgraded utility buildings</td><td>Solid door with lower maintenance than wood</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d02-02\">4-Lite Glass Slab Door</a></td><td>$750</td><td>Utility or garden rooms needing modest daylight</td><td>Light increases while privacy decreases</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d02-03\">6-Lite Glass Slab Door</a></td><td>$750</td><td>Workshops and hobby spaces</td><td>Moderate daylight without a highly glazed appearance</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d02-04\">9-Lite Glass Slab Door</a></td><td>$780</td><td>Garden buildings, studios and hobby spaces</td><td>More inviting entry; review privacy</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d02-05\">11-Lite Glass Slab Door</a></td><td>$810</td><td>Brighter hobby and studio spaces</td><td>Good visual upgrade for a front-facing wall</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d02-06\">15-Lite Glass Slab Door</a></td><td>$930</td><td>Studios, garden rooms and light-focused spaces</td><td>Highest daylight within this slab-door group</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d02-07\">Double Fiberglass Slab Doors</a></td><td>$1,260</td><td>Wide access with durable door faces</td><td>Useful where wood character is not the priority</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d02-08\">Double Colonial Fiberglass Doors</a></td><td>$1,500</td><td>Premium garden, workshop and visible elevations</td><td>More finished appearance than plain double slabs</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"adf-price-note\">Glass-lite options remain part of the fiberglass slab family; they are not treated as a separate door category.</p>\n</section>\n<div class=\"asi-photo-group\"><div class=\"asi-photo-head\"><p class=\"asi-photo-eyebrow\">Door Appearance Reference \u00b7 Photography To Be Added</p><h4>Compare the Actual Door Configurations</h4><p>Each position is reserved for a photograph of the exact door option named below. Photographs will be supplied by Appalachian Sheds; no conceptual substitute is shown.</p></div><div class=\"asi-door-gallery\"><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d02-01\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: Single Fiberglass Slab Door\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D02-01 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>Single Fiberglass Slab Door</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d02-02\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: 4-Lite Glass Slab Door\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D02-02 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>4-Lite Glass Slab Door</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d02-03\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: 6-Lite Glass Slab Door\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D02-03 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>6-Lite Glass Slab Door</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d02-04\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: 9-Lite Glass Slab Door\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D02-04 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>9-Lite Glass Slab Door</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d02-05\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: 11-Lite Glass Slab Door\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D02-05 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>11-Lite Glass Slab Door</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d02-06\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: 15-Lite Glass Slab Door\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D02-06 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>15-Lite Glass Slab Door</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d02-07\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: Double Fiberglass Slab Doors\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D02-07 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>Double Fiberglass Slab Doors</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d02-08\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: Double Colonial Fiberglass Doors\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D02-08 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>Double Colonial Fiberglass Doors</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure></div></div></section>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"asi-door-prehung-fiberglass-title\" class=\"adf-option\" id=\"asi-door-prehung-fiberglass\">\n<div class=\"adf-option-head\">\n<div class=\"adf-option-copy\">\n<span class=\"adf-mini\">Door Option 03</span>\n<h3 id=\"asi-door-prehung-fiberglass-title\">Prehung Fiberglass Entry Doors \u2014 Residential House Doors</h3>\n<p>A prehung fiberglass entry door is a complete residential-style entry assembly. The door slab is supplied with its jamb system and is planned around a coordinated threshold, weatherstripping, hinges and latch preparation. This is the closest option to a conventional exterior house door.</p>\n<p>It is particularly appropriate for backyard offices, studios, finished interiors, poolside rooms and other buildings where the entry should feel more like a small residential room than a utility shed.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"adf-option-character\">\n<span class=\"adf-character-label\">Architectural Character</span>\n<h3>Residential. Finished. Secure. Familiar.</h3>\n<p>The strongest choice when comfort, daily pedestrian use, weather sealing and a finished-room entry experience matter more than traditional shed-door character.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"adf-two-grid\">\n<section class=\"adf-panel\">\n<h4>Typical Prehung Entry Assembly</h4>\n<ul class=\"adf-list\">\n<li>Factory-assembled fiberglass door slab and jamb system</li>\n<li>Integrated threshold and weatherstripping</li>\n<li>Residential-style hinge and latch preparation</li>\n<li>Properly framed rough opening sized for the complete unit</li>\n<li>WRB, flashing and trim integrated around the opening</li>\n<li>Keyed lockset and deadbolt options where selected</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"adf-panel\">\n<h4>Available Design Directions</h4>\n<ul class=\"adf-list\">\n<li>Solid residential fiberglass entry doors</li>\n<li>9-lite, 11-lite and 15-lite glazed configurations</li>\n<li>Double residential fiberglass door configurations</li>\n<li>Craftsman-style entries</li>\n<li>Farmhouse-style entries</li>\n<li>Modern design-forward fiberglass entries</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</div>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"adf-prehung-price-title\" class=\"adf-pricing\">\n<div class=\"adf-pricing-head\">\n<h4 id=\"adf-prehung-price-title\">Residential-Style Fiberglass Door Planning Prices</h4>\n<p>These installed planning prices are preserved from the supplied Appalachian Sheds source information.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"adf-table-wrap\">\n<table class=\"adf-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\">Residential Entry Option</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Installed Planning Price</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Best For</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Planning Note</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d03-01\">Solid House Door</a></td><td>$1,500</td><td>Offices, studios and privacy-focused rooms</td><td>Residential feel without glass exposure</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d03-02\">House Door \u2014 9-Lite Glass</a></td><td>$1,740</td><td>Backyard offices and studios</td><td>Balanced daylight and entry presence</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d03-03\">House Door \u2014 11-Lite Glass</a></td><td>$1,740</td><td>Studios, garden rooms and poolside spaces</td><td>Light-forward residential appearance</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d03-04\">House Door \u2014 15-Lite Glass</a></td><td>$1,860</td><td>Bright studios and garden retreats</td><td>Privacy and security should be reviewed</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d03-05\">Double Solid House Doors</a></td><td>$2,754</td><td>Premium finished spaces needing wide access</td><td>Strong visual entry without glass exposure</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d03-06\">Double House Doors \u2014 9-Lite</a></td><td>$3,114</td><td>Studios, retreats and visible elevations</td><td>French-style feel with controlled glazing</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d03-07\">Double House Doors \u2014 11-Lite</a></td><td>$3,114</td><td>Finished flex spaces and poolside buildings</td><td>High curb appeal and daylight</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d03-08\">Double House Doors \u2014 15-Lite</a></td><td>$3,354</td><td>Premium light-focused spaces</td><td>Highest glazing; privacy planning matters</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d03-09\">Craftsman Style \u2014 Factory White</a></td><td>$2,154</td><td>Backyard offices and refined cottage buildings</td><td>Architectural entry without excessive decoration</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d03-10\">Farmhouse Style \u2014 Factory White</a></td><td>$2,154</td><td>Farmhouse, cottage and garden buildings</td><td>Pairs naturally with board-and-batten</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d03-11\">Modern Spotlight \u2014 Factory White</a></td><td>$3,660</td><td>Modern studios, offices and specialty buildings</td><td>Most design-forward source-listed house-door option</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"adf-price-note\">A residential-style door changes the entry experience, but it does not by itself change the legal use or classification of the building.</p>\n</section>\n<div class=\"asi-photo-group\"><div class=\"asi-photo-head\"><p class=\"asi-photo-eyebrow\">Door Appearance Reference \u00b7 Photography To Be Added</p><h4>Compare the Actual Door Configurations</h4><p>Each position is reserved for a photograph of the exact door option named below. Photographs will be supplied by Appalachian Sheds; no conceptual substitute is shown.</p></div><div class=\"asi-door-gallery\"><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d03-01\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: Solid House Door\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D03-01 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>Solid House Door</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d03-02\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: House Door \u2014 9-Lite Glass\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D03-02 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>House Door \u2014 9-Lite Glass</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d03-03\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: House Door \u2014 11-Lite Glass\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D03-03 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>House Door \u2014 11-Lite Glass</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d03-04\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: House Door \u2014 15-Lite Glass\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D03-04 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>House Door \u2014 15-Lite Glass</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d03-05\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: Double Solid House Doors\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D03-05 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>Double Solid House Doors</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d03-06\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: Double House Doors \u2014 9-Lite\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D03-06 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>Double House Doors \u2014 9-Lite</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d03-07\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: Double House Doors \u2014 11-Lite\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D03-07 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>Double House Doors \u2014 11-Lite</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d03-08\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: Double House Doors \u2014 15-Lite\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D03-08 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>Double House Doors \u2014 15-Lite</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d03-09\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: Craftsman Style \u2014 Factory White\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D03-09 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>Craftsman Style \u2014 Factory White</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d03-10\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: Farmhouse Style \u2014 Factory White\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D03-10 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>Farmhouse Style \u2014 Factory White</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d03-11\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: Modern Spotlight \u2014 Factory White\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D03-11 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>Modern Spotlight \u2014 Factory White</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure></div></div></section>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"asi-door-carriage-title\" class=\"adf-option\" id=\"asi-door-carriage\">\n<div class=\"adf-option-head\">\n<div class=\"adf-option-copy\">\n<span class=\"adf-mini\">Door Option 04</span>\n<h3 id=\"asi-door-carriage-title\">Architectural Carriage-Style Double Doors</h3>\n<p>Architectural carriage-style double doors are the premium choice when the entry itself should become a defining part of the exterior design. Traditional proportions, substantial trim and carefully selected hardware can reinforce Appalachian, barn, cottage or farmhouse character while still providing practical wide access.</p>\n<p>The supplied source identifies carriage wood doors as a highly selected premium door direction. Because this category is architectural rather than one universal factory product, final material, glazing, hardware and finish details are confirmed with the selected building design.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"adf-option-character\">\n<span class=\"adf-character-label\">Architectural Character</span>\n<h3>Crafted. Traditional. Distinctive. Premium.</h3>\n<p>Best when the door should contribute as much to the building's identity as the roofline, siding, windows and trim.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"adf-two-grid\">\n<section class=\"adf-panel\">\n<h4>Common Design Elements</h4>\n<ul class=\"adf-list\">\n<li>Paired wide-access configuration</li>\n<li>Traditional carriage or barn-inspired proportions</li>\n<li>Cross-bracing or other architectural detailing where specified</li>\n<li>Optional glazing or transom treatment where appropriate</li>\n<li>Substantial exterior hinges and coordinated hardware</li>\n<li>Threshold and ramp coordinated with actual equipment access</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"adf-panel\">\n<h4>Best Uses</h4>\n<ul class=\"adf-list\">\n<li>Premium Classic and Signature buildings</li>\n<li>Barn-inspired sheds and workshops</li>\n<li>Garden buildings facing the home or patio</li>\n<li>Custom cottages and backyard destination buildings</li>\n<li>Projects where curb appeal is a primary objective</li>\n<li>Wide-access storage where basic utility doors would underserve the architecture</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</div>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"adf-carriage-price-title\" class=\"adf-pricing\">\n<div class=\"adf-pricing-head\">\n<h4 id=\"adf-carriage-price-title\">Carriage-Style Door Planning Price</h4>\n<p>The source information provides a specific installed planning price for the carriage wood door configuration.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"adf-table-wrap\">\n<table class=\"adf-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\">Carriage Door Option</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Installed Planning Price</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Best For</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Planning Note</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"#door-photo-d04-01\">Carriage Wood Doors</a></td><td>$1,500</td><td>Premium visible elevations, barn-style and carriage-style buildings</td><td>Strong character when siding, trim and roofline support the design</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"adf-price-note\">More elaborate custom carriage-style configurations are priced according to the final material, glazing, hardware, finish and construction scope.</p>\n</section>\n<div class=\"asi-photo-group\"><div class=\"asi-photo-head\"><p class=\"asi-photo-eyebrow\">Door Appearance Reference \u00b7 Photography To Be Added</p><h4>Compare the Actual Door Configurations</h4><p>Each position is reserved for a photograph of the exact door option named below. Photographs will be supplied by Appalachian Sheds; no conceptual substitute is shown.</p></div><div class=\"asi-door-gallery\"><figure class=\"asi-door-photo-card\" id=\"door-photo-d04-01\"><div aria-label=\"Photograph pending: Carriage Wood Doors\" class=\"asi-door-photo-placeholder\" role=\"img\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"asi-photo-outline\">\u25a7</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-label\">IMAGE D04-01 \u00b7 PHOTO TO BE SUPPLIED</span><span class=\"asi-placeholder-subtitle\">Approved product photograph only</span></div><figcaption><strong>Carriage Wood Doors</strong><span>Actual installed door appearance \u00b7 source-listed option</span></figcaption></figure></div></div></section>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"adf-planning-title\" class=\"adf-planning\">\n<div class=\"adf-section-head\">\n<span>Plan the Entry Before We Frame the Wall</span>\n<h3 id=\"adf-planning-title\">Door Decisions Affect More Than the Door</h3>\n<p>Opening width, swing, threshold, ramp, weather protection, security and glazing should be resolved together.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"adf-plan-grid\">\n<div class=\"adf-plan-card\"><strong>Opening Width</strong><span>Measure the largest mower, cart, workbench, appliance or equipment that must pass through\u2014with comfortable clearance.</span></div>\n<div class=\"adf-plan-card\"><strong>Swing &amp; Clearance</strong><span>Check exterior approach, interior wall use, shelving, workbenches and nearby landscaping before choosing the swing.</span></div>\n<div class=\"adf-plan-card\"><strong>Threshold &amp; Ramp</strong><span>Coordinate threshold height, ramp width, slope and landing so the access path actually matches the door opening.</span></div>\n<div class=\"adf-plan-card\"><strong>Glass &amp; Privacy</strong><span>More glass improves daylight and entry presence but changes privacy, security and interior visibility.</span></div>\n<div class=\"adf-plan-card\"><strong>Flashing</strong><span>Door-head, jamb and sill water-management details must coordinate with the siding and WRB system.</span></div>\n<div class=\"adf-plan-card\"><strong>Weather Sealing</strong><span>Threshold sealing, sweeps and weatherstripping are especially important on finished or comfort-oriented buildings.</span></div>\n<div class=\"adf-plan-card\"><strong>Hardware</strong><span>Exterior hinges, locksets, latches and deadbolts should match the door family, weight, use and security expectation.</span></div>\n<div class=\"adf-plan-card\"><strong>Exterior Finish</strong><span>Door material determines whether paint, stain, sealing or manufacturer-specific finishing instructions apply.</span></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"adf-compare-title\" class=\"adf-compare\">\n<div class=\"adf-compare-head\">\n<span>Final Door Comparison</span>\n<h3 id=\"adf-compare-title\">Four Door Families \u2014 Four Different Entry Experiences</h3>\n<p>On smaller screens, swipe or scroll horizontally to see the complete comparison.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"adf-table-wrap\">\n<table class=\"adf-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\">Door Family</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Primary Purpose</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Construction Style</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Architectural Character</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Typical Uses</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Key Planning Issue</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Wood Doors</td>\n<td>Traditional shed and wide-access entry</td>\n<td>Wood door construction integrated with the building opening</td>\n<td>Most traditional / Appalachian</td>\n<td>Storage, garden, cottage and barn-inspired buildings</td>\n<td>Finish maintenance, hinge support and moisture protection</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fiberglass Solid Slab with Exterior Hinges</td>\n<td>Durable shed-style access with lower-maintenance door faces</td>\n<td>Fiberglass slab mounted in a building-integrated exterior-hinged opening</td>\n<td>Clean and practical without a house-door appearance</td>\n<td>Workshops, hobby buildings, storage and utility structures</td>\n<td>Hinge sizing, threshold, swing and ramp width</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Prehung Fiberglass Entry Door</td>\n<td>Residential-style everyday entry</td>\n<td>Complete door, jamb, threshold and weatherstripping assembly</td>\n<td>Most residential / finished</td>\n<td>Studios, offices, pool houses, garden rooms and premium buildings</td>\n<td>Rough opening, flashing, threshold and door swing</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Architectural Carriage-Style Double Doors</td>\n<td>Wide access plus premium architectural presence</td>\n<td>Project-specific paired architectural door system</td>\n<td>Appalachian / barn / cottage focal point</td>\n<td>Premium sheds, workshops, custom cottages and Signature buildings</td>\n<td>Material, hardware, finish, threshold and detailing</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"adf-compare-note\">Door sizes, materials, manufacturers, glass patterns, hardware, finish requirements and standard-versus-upgrade status vary by building model and product availability. Final specifications and pricing are confirmed in the written project scope.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"adf-finish\">\n<h3>Door Finishing &amp; Weather-Protection Responsibility</h3>\n<p>Wood, fiberglass slab, prehung fiberglass and architectural carriage-style systems do not all share the same field-finishing requirements. Wood doors normally require an appropriate protective finish and ongoing maintenance, while fiberglass products may be supplied primed, factory-finished or subject to manufacturer-specific finishing instructions.</p>\n<p>Required flashing, threshold sealing, weatherstripping and construction sealants are part of proper installation where applicable. Decorative finish caulking, field painting or staining is controlled by the selected door system and the written project scope.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"adf-cta\">\n<div class=\"adf-cta-copy\">\n<span>Choose Function Before Style</span>\n<h3>Start With the Largest Item That Must Pass Through the Opening</h3>\n<p>Once the access requirement is established, Appalachian Sheds can help match it with the appropriate wood, fiberglass slab, prehung fiberglass or architectural carriage-style door system for the selected building.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"adf-cta-side\">\n<a href=\"/options-upgrades/\">Explore Options &amp; Upgrades</a>\n<a class=\"adf-ghost\" href=\"tel:15133792421\">Call Edwin \u00b7 (513) 379-2421</a>\n</div>\n</section>\n</div>\n</section>"} />
